# en-US: only the messages whose words differ from the house English (en-GB).
# Everything else falls back to English.

# Words a person might type into the Settings search to find the appearance page; separate them with spaces.
settings-appearance-keywords = color colors color colors accent theme themes look skin glass dark light mode sunshine bright icons font cursor pointer screen reader blind read aloud accessibility labels tooltips names pointing

# Introduction under the heading of the appearance page, and the words behind the page i.
settings-appearance-help = Light or dark, colors, icons, fonts, the pointer and reading the screen aloud. Some programs only notice after they are reopened.

# Small words on a theme's tile when Trindle made some of its colours clearer.
settings-appearance-corrected = Some colors were made clearer to read.

# Words behind the i of the Theme card.
settings-appearance-theme-about = A theme is a whole look in one file: colors, corners, sizes and room. Press one to try it: every Trindle window changes at once, and the look you had comes back by itself in 30 seconds unless you press Keep, so a theme that cannot be read never stays. A theme that has a dark look and a light one has Dark and Light beside its picture; Light is easier to see in bright sunshine, and apps from Apps take it the next time they open. A theme with one look has no such buttons. Your highlight color stays your own in every theme. A theme you add is only read, never run, and words it would make hard to read are made clearer. From a terminal, trindle-settings --theme default always brings Trindle's own look back.

# Spoken description of the small dot that shows the colour typed.
settings-appearance-dot = The color typed

# Spoken name of the box for typing a colour as a hex code; the example is a code.
settings-appearance-hex-spoken = Any color, as a hex code such as #fbc711

# Heading of the line for typing any colour.
settings-appearance-any-colour = Any color

# Title of the Colour card.
settings-appearance-colour-title = Color

# Words behind the i of the Colour card.
settings-appearance-colour-about = The highlight marks buttons, switches, the filling ring and where you are. Trindle's own windows change at once; the ring on its next opening. A color too dark to see on a card is lightened until it can be read, and in a light look one too pale is darkened. Dark or Light is chosen on a theme's own tile, under Theme.

